=== 3. the fair coin: no zero approaches it ===
      profile      k      min |z - 1/2|   min over (0,1)
         odds     32       0.5176543967       3.00000000
         odds     64       0.5046417828       3.00000000
         odds     96       0.5020919026       3.00000000
       primes     32       0.5015462470       5.34928793
       primes     64       0.4972006464       5.34928793
       primes     96       0.4973287735       5.34928793
    geometric     32       0.0520250691      34.00000000
    geometric     64       0.0252946762      66.00000000
    geometric     96       0.0166986496      98.00000000
   Gamma^(q) is real and >= 3 on (0,1) by thm:fair, so no real zero is possible at all;
   the column above says the complex zeros do not approach q = 1/2 either

=== 4. the other accumulation point: the primitive sixth roots of unity ===
       k   min |z - e^{i pi/3}|            |z|          |1-z|
      24         0.044789385711     1.03903012     1.03903012
      48         0.022098798362     1.01919802     1.01919802
      72         0.014668831827     1.01273014     1.01273014
      96         0.010978017832     1.00952216     1.00952216
   1 - q + q^2 vanishes exactly where |q| = |1-q| = 1, on the boundary of both discs,
   which is why the k-dependent terms never become negligible there

